interpretations surrounding the Ring of Nestor.", "requirement": "should", "supported_boundary": "Evidence from Eliopoulos 2013 and other academic discussions 
shows a long‑standing scholarly debate over the Ring of Nestor’s authenticity and iconographic interpretation. Sources note that authenticity was questioned, 
with accusations of forgery (especially involving the Gillierons) dating back to the 1920s and framed within broader concerns about Aegean forgeries. Recent 
scholarship, including Eliopoulos and Vlachopoulos, re‑examines iconography and technical features, presenting new technical observations and comparative 
iconographic evidence that support authenticity and emphasize the importance of iconographic analysis amid contradictory technical assessments. One cited 
statement notes that this tendency to see the ring (and the Ring of Minos) as fake has been ‘reassessed completely in favour of their authenticity.’ Other 
