[AIMessage → tool] create_analysis({'text': 'Given the current evidence basis, a Wikipedia-style article on the Ring of Nestor should: (1) define it as a 
Creto-Mycenaean gold signet ring from the early Late Bronze Age (16th–15th century BC), emphasizing its large size and place within Aegean glyptic; (2) provide 
a concise, neutral overview of its complex figural iconography (world-tree scene, guardian/scorpion motif, populous composition) and summarize major scholarly 
interpretations, especially Eliopoulos’s apotropaic scorpion reading and alternative cosmological or deity-centered interpretations; (3) describe physical 
characteristics with cited dimensions and craftsmanship details while making clear that current evidence does not identify a secure present museum location or 
detailed provenance history; (4) explain that discovery history and archaeological context remain incompletely documented in accessible non-Wikipedia sources, 
with only tentative, medium-confidence links to early 20th-century discoveries, and avoid over-claiming specific tomb or assemblage contexts; and (5) devote a 
